JoseEduardoMartins/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JoseEduardoMartins/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JoseEduardoMartins/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JoseEduardoMartins/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JoseEduardoMartins","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JoseEduardoMartins/react-step-flow/commits/85c41529d7cd79b9811082c983285e8c537b8948/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-16T23:34:53Z","email":"m4rt1ns.jose@gmail.com","name":"Eduardo Martins"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-16T23:34:53Z","email":"m4rt1ns.jose@gmail.com","name":"Eduardo Martins"},"message":"fix: keep side-placed tooltips on their axis instead of flipping onto the target\n\nA tooltip anchored to a target at the top edge of the viewport (e.g. a right-side\ndrawer''s header) with placement \"left\" is centered vertically on that target and\noverflows the top on the cross axis. With flip''s cross-axis check enabled it\ntreated that as a reason to fall back to the perpendicular axis\n(fallbackAxisSideDirection), landing the tooltip at \"bottom\" — directly over the\npanel it was meant to sit beside.\n\nDisable flip''s crossAxis check so a side placement stays on its axis; `shift`\n(already present) slides the tooltip along the cross axis to keep it in view.\nReproduced in a real browser against a sliding right-side drawer: placement went\nfrom \"bottom\" (over the panel) to \"left\" (beside it). Guarded by a useFloatingStep\ntest asserting flip is configured with crossAxis:false.","tree":{"sha":"8dbbbd9cf0405f44367a83dc25610107812496a8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JoseEduardoMartins/react-step-flow/git/trees/8dbbbd9cf0405f44367a83dc25610107812496a8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JoseEduardoMartins/react-step-flow/git/commits/85c41529d7cd79b9811082c983285e8c537b8948","verification":{"payl