"subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ssbingo/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ssbingo","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ssbingo/ioBroker.pondpump/commits/9585962af808c092782c442493d13d693229dd42/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-26T14:36:01Z","email":"s.sternitzke@online.de","name":"ssbingo"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-26T14:36:01Z","email":"s.sternitzke@online.de","name":"ssbingo"},"message":"Phase 9: real per-pump admin tabs (dynamic, native jsonConfig)\n\nRework the scheduler UI from inner MUI tabs inside one field to genuine,\ndynamically-appearing admin tabs — one per pump that has scheduling enabled —\nso each pump has its own page (room for future temperature/weather params).\n\n- admin/jsonConfig.json: top-level `tabs` — Connection · Schedules · pump0..9.\n  Each pump panel''s `hidden` and `label` are derived live from native.schedules\n  (enabled pump ids, sorted by device number → slot index); json-config\n  recomputes them on every data change, so a tab appears/disappears the moment\n  its pump is toggled. Labels show the pump name via a ${...} pattern.\n- PondpumpScheduler.tsx: one component, two roles via schema.custom.pumpSlot —\n  no pumpSlot => the enable list (Schedules tab); a number => that pump''s editor\n  (base power + schedule table + live overlap validation). Enabling caches the\n  pump name into native.schedules for the tab label. No config side-effects:\n  tab visibility is a pure function of the stored schedules.\n- schedule core: add optional `name` (UI metadata; backend ignores it).\n- i18n: +2 keys (\"Schedules for %s\", pump-list intro) across all 11 languages.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"1feeff1f8b5c47c9a14ff35caad31f00058abfd0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ssbingo/ioBroker.pondpump/git/trees/1feeff1f8b5c47c9a14ff35caad31f00058abfd0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/rep