a50c338266923f521","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hoeken/signalk-container-helper/commits/11b40ba653e1c3a76a9eb43a50c338266923f521"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/86628605?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dirkwa","id":86628605,"login":"dirkwa","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg2NjI4NjA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hoeken/signalk-container-helper/commits/db227c68b14d64cce3c960b8f054f2913d1cada5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-30T17:36:08Z","email":"86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Dirk Wahrheit"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-30T17:36:08Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs: mirror the named-volume scope rule (#56)\n\n* docs: mirror the named-volume scope rule\n\nsignalk-container now refuses a named volume attached above the directory\na mount field requests: volumes cannot be subpath-mounted, so a parent\nvolume would hand the container its entire contents rather than the\ndirectory that was asked for. That case throws at `ensureRunning`.\n\nThe mirror carried no trace of this, so a consumer reading it planned for\nan over-broad mount that will instead fail. Documented on both mount\nfields, on `resolveSignalkDataMount`, and in the README, with the escape\nhatch (`resolveMount()`, which reports `subPath`) named each time.\n\nPinned in the doc-anchor test, the same mechanism that caught the #35\ndrift. No version numbers: the upstream release is not cut yet.\n\nRefs hoeken/signalk-container-helper#55, dirkwa/signalk-container#261\n\n* docs: name the compat-API mechanism behind the rule\n\n* docs: say accepted-and-ignored, not cannot\n\n* docs: scope the subpath note to podman","tree":{"sha":"b021e2788d9d5ccee3cb993659994ac3a52dbc57","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hoeken/signalk-container-helper/git/trees/b021e2788d9d5ccee3cb993659994ac3a52dbc57"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hoeken/signalk-container-helper/git/commits/db227c68b14d64cce3c960b8f054f2913d1cada5","verification":{"payload":"tree b021e2788d9d5ccee3cb993659994ac3a52dbc57\nparent 8dd131c1d83d5041e72353d7e32e30c458f0bb2c\nauthor Dirk Wahrheit <86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com> 1788111368 +1200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788111368 +1200\n\ndocs: mirror the named-volume scope rule (#56)\n\n* docs: mirror the named-volume scope rule\n\nsignalk-container now refuses a named volume attached above the directory\na mount field requests: volumes cannot be subpath-mounted, so a parent\nvolume would hand the container its entire contents rather than the\ndirectory that was asked for. That case throws at `ensureRunning`.\n\nThe mirror carried no trace of this, so a consumer reading it planned for\nan over-broad mount that will instead fail. Documented on both mount\nfields, on `resolveSignalkDataMount`, and in the README, with the escape\nhatch (`resolveMount()`, which reports `subPath`) named each time.\n\nPinned in the doc-anchor test, the same mechanism that caught the #35\ndrift. No version numbers: the upstream release is not cut yet.\n\nRefs hoeken/signalk-container-helper#55, dirkwa/signalk-container#261\n\n* docs: name the compat-API mechanism behind the rule\n\n* docs: say accepted-and-ignored, not cannot\n\n* docs: scope the subpath note to podman","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqlGoICRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAGJEQAB8Ry211yX7BpIqnUm/TJmJM\nYYuqX5ZbqA0C4sAOzA0q/JFw/9NnoQk7UQ5z3IpHCQ4lqqwr9DKk8TNSFl3ukXVV\n3317ke+RIw0D4yuLfFTrVOBQ9CK/VIqaTQSJ+UrFGIKFTieW0zUPgD6jNFQQN+9i\ntA1N2WER/5Ox7RjLakNipnkZ+jvhzgIm+HQa6LXQFIFrB8RZBs4JLO8t4HVXIgf3\naCpo9v4kh9Vfpv6DMd5YLzlF0FtIfRoj3apUbekUFGa0ii99qSF2AoEFVA++SXAQ\ntAw2iMx/GyXwwcVQRXLdMgHmMITWiFmaLyuo4rQp7kXvGk417UBeMlTFzNs6nzNm\nagDbF9n1BiRdr/anh2D2NsoZUN/SA/HjYZ9xSMiZ61QbNy+GkE2pq5W51klVQmI3\nQ6d7GuyU5XsFYLUveJSEjj00j4Anfd0sgPiVebROdQoD+o+Xv5gs2Rl3y+Lk7VMr\nExZydNkkxBGC3TuOr63SfdXxYUvjs3NMQN6AASgT+GTJIF3VBxlQSyn2PYFRuI3w\nZWpkYGlC9UpECz0B9S6PASoTHi/3bIsXMOtSQ2mhEkE0BO+eUgfsKg3ZeZAN7oCi\nz6cjw2yUASRz4rpFAd8aWh1SA/NXQG4nNXlaf73HwbusLZ/6lZHogBxygkN+kxZK\nebQSveuWrX59uRuoKpeX\n=5gCJ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-30T17:36:09Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/hoeken/signalk-container-helper/commit/db227c68b14d64cce3c960