l":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dirkwa","id":86628605,"login":"dirkwa","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg2NjI4NjA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hoeken/signalk-container-helper/commits/78b1b60bcbe37a0cfd7aa624194c0db5f68d5de0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-24T05:02:42Z","email":"dirkwahrheit@gmail.com","name":"Dirk Wahrheit"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-24T05:02:42Z","email":"dirkwahrheit@gmail.com","name":"Dirk Wahrheit"},"message":"chore(release): 0.10.0","tree":{"sha":"f46bef7fcdd784b45b5a5a21da8e46cbfaf81da5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hoeken/signalk-container-helper/git/trees/f46bef7fcdd784b45b5a5a21da8e46cbfaf81da5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hoeken/signalk-container-helper/git/commits/78b1b60bcbe37a0cfd7aa624194c0db5f68d5de0","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/86628605?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dirkwa","id":86628605,"login":"dirkwa","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg2NjI4NjA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/hoeken/signalk-container-helper/commit/78b1b60bcbe37a0cfd7aa624194c0db5f68d5de0","node_id":"C_kwDOTgx649oAKDc4YjFiNjBiY2JlMzdhMGNmZDdhYTYyNDE5NGMwZGI1ZjY4ZDVkZTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/hoeken/signalk-container-helper/commit/a5742bad29e521c304965e889fce3e406f9f9171","sha":"a5742bad29e521c304965e889fce3e406f9f9171","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hoeken/signalk-container-helper/commits/a5742bad29e521c304965e889fce3e406f9f9171"}],"sha":"78b1b60bcbe37a0cfd7aa624194c0db5f68d5de0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hoeken/signalk-container-helper/commits/78b1b60bcbe37a0cfd7aa624194c0db5f68d5de0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/86628605?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dirkwa","id":86628605,"login":"dirkwa","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg2NjI4NjA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hoeken/signalk-container-helper/commits/a5742bad29e521c304965e889fce3e406f9f9171/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-24T04:59:57Z","email":"86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Dirk Wahrheit"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-24T04:59:57Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(schema): hide the external URL field while the container is managed (#50)\n\n* feat(schema): hide the external URL field while the container is managed\n\nThe URL field rendered unconditionally, so an operator running a managed\ncontainer saw a field that does nothing — including its \"traffic leaves this\nhost\" warning, which is alarming when nothing is leaving the host.\n\nmanagedModeSchema now also returns a `dependencies` fragment that renders the\nfield only when the toggle is off. Additive: a consumer that omits it keeps\nthe current always-visible behaviour.\n\nUses JSON Schema dependencies rather than uiSchema `ui:disabled`, because a\nplugin''s uiSchema is fetched once when the form loads: a greyed-out field\nwould stay greyed until a page reload, so flipping the toggle would appear to\ndo nothing. RJSF re-evaluates dependencies on every change.\n\nVerified against the same @rjsf/validator-ajv8 the Signal K admin UI ships:\nmanaged and unset both render without the field, false renders with it.\n\n* fix(schema): make the hiding actually work, and keep the type\n\nSelf-audit caught that the feature did not do what it claimed. RJSF renders\neverything in `properties` regardless of what a dependency says, so with\n`externalUrl` in both places — which is exactly what the README instructed —\nthe field never hid. My test had asserted on the fragment shape rather than\non the documented arrangement, so it passed while the documented setup\nreproduced the reported bug.\n\nThe field has to be left out of `properties`. That costs the type: TypeBox\nderives Static<> from `properties` alone, so `settings.externalUrl` would\nstop compiling for every consumer. WithExternalUrl<T, U> adds it back,\nkeeping the awkwardness in the library rather than repeated in each plugin.\n\nVerified end to end against the same @rjsf/validator-ajv8 the admin UI ships:\nwith the documented arrangement the field is absent when managed or unset and\npresent when self-hosted, while a full TypeBox consumer — schema, Config type\nand SCHEMA_DEFAULTS — compiles clean.\n\nThe new test asserts the managed branch contributes nothing but the\ndiscriminator, which is the property that was silently untrue.","tree":{"sha":"7b89672120db637ec0dfb83f8eec5af9a1fea52a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hoeken/signalk-container-helper/git/trees/7b89672120db637ec0dfb83f8eec5af9a1fea52a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hoeken/signalk-container-helper/git/commits/a5742bad29e521c304965e889fce3e406f9f9171","verification":{"payload":"tree 7b89672120db637ec0dfb83f8eec5af9a1fea52a\nparent 8073a217cc5f9428a8533c3f586336b3e615f99d\nauthor Dirk Wahrheit <86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com> 1787547597 +1200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787547597 +1200\n\nfeat(schema): hide the external URL field while the container is managed (#50)\n\n* feat(schema): hide the external URL field while the container is managed\n\nThe URL field rendered unconditionally, so an operator running a managed\ncontainer saw a field that does nothing — including its \"traffic leaves this\nhost\" warning, which is alarming when nothing is leaving the host.\n\nmanagedModeSchema now also returns a `dependencies` fragment that renders the\nfield only when the toggle is off. Additive: a consumer that omits it keeps\nthe current always-visible behaviour.\n\nUses JSON Schema dependencies rather than uiSchema `ui:disabled`, because a\nplugin''s uiSchema is fetched once when the form loads: a greyed-out field\nwould stay greyed until a page reload, so flipping the toggle would appear to\ndo nothing. RJSF re-evaluates dependencies on every change.\n\nVerified against the same @rjsf/validator-ajv8 the Signal K admin UI ships:\nmanaged and unset both render without the field, false renders with it.\n\n* fix(schema): make the hiding actually work, and keep the type\n\nSelf-audit caught that the feature did not do what it claimed. RJSF renders\neverything in `properties` regardless of what a dependency says, so with\n`externalUrl` in both places — which is exactly what the README instructed —\nthe field never hid. My test had asserted on the fragment shape rather than\non the documented arrangement, so it passed while the documented setup\nreproduced the reported bug.\n\nThe field has to be left out of `properties`. That costs the type: TypeBox\nderives Static<> from `properties` alone, so `settings.externalUrl` would\nstop compiling for every consumer. WithExternalUrl<T, U> adds it back,\nkeeping the awkwardness in the library rather than repeated in each plugin.\n\nVerified end to end against the same @rjsf/validator-ajv8 the admin UI ships:\nwith the documented arrangement the field is absent when managed or unset and\npresent when self-hosted, while a full TypeBox consumer — schema, Config type\nand SCHEMA_DEFAULTS — compiles clean.\n\nThe new test asserts the managed branch contributes nothing but the\ndiscriminator, which is the property that was silently untrue.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqi8/NCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAQaQQAI0bY6KnMRf/Wb8OtRiD7ghy\ncA1HsEi9ZI5IUWXHk+X9I5RpmvFWu+3sndixWBXB+dteC8PeXNmBGQaEU6mbZKcR\n3+CboTAVVqSd2Q8pcfg9/I0ZWLOm694unOzBxsZh/QIXMrx1dlm51s7eh2Cm7gy6\no3pX6HTV5m+RmeZ9ATPUDWC2ts3fl8hzw8jCTNYBwkdrlnuOyPWUs7ghRKu/qud2\nW8FijACL1stGY8eiLcUHeR2fGwjFcB2krM005LvLaYzE/EscnQ1aPPvKv2J5zK2a\nqmUufJk0/uZLKHZOXMZKEUkwhlpNzeuejEfSg5RIEVPdagEeA7kemRnyWZQKZsAN\nv6JnogDDA5N4aeY0l+uQC31fSsQDdWoMVCDBurKjxfZgn0yKvFeAgA+ZXrPuqd1g\nUZ15dK5B/fi0nsyEg3Dts3Y1DcscS53DKVj8hk/hJGzh6qjDLDKVeZkhXXec2pm8\nChTwb0WMNDgXoSs30b7wG+YcVYkqsgNa9msO