stom `urlFieldName`\ncarries through instead of widening to string. Runtime output is unchanged.\n\nPinned in types-contract.test-d.ts, which fails compilation on the\nregression rather than letting it reach a consumer.","tree":{"sha":"288561440910a84cda06103e03665d339d422566","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hoeken/signalk-container-helper/git/trees/288561440910a84cda06103e03665d339d422566"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hoeken/signalk-container-helper/git/commits/0ac470e5c79d36b11f73b54f2dfeb1d8b81d6cae","verification":{"payload":"tree 288561440910a84cda06103e03665d339d422566\nparent aee9aace42d470bfbfa9124d8d7d826e4621c1bc\nauthor Dirk Wahrheit <86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com> 1787512423 +1200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787512423 +1200\n\nfix: keep the key names in managedModeSchema defaults (#46)\n\n`defaults` is meant to be spread straight into a consumer''s typed\nSCHEMA_DEFAULTS, but `Record<string, boolean | string>` erases which keys it\nsupplies — so the spread does not satisfy the consumer''s Config and every\nconsumer hits \"missing the following properties: managedContainer,\nexternalUrl\". Found on the first real migration (signalk-tailscale).\n\nMake the type generic over the URL field name so a custom `urlFieldName`\ncarries through instead of widening to string. Runtime output is unchanged.\n\nPinned in types-contract.test-d.ts, which fails compilation on the\nregression rather than letting it reach a consumer.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqi0ZnCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAM3AQAGNdwCWmAycK8TUgVNkJPFPG\n38zn1dXo+UivWpGj6bYgXnwgZVQ7LCy1a1yeYsjvY6A79W1QRoHYeSeW6ijRQDvI\nzij+chKyVRVpFvAwJ5rlLf/tbDHJ7wdtGdiR/qQHUeyJg60gluXjVqn8+Tyd7Bwg\nsnIBMrftbHONMw6J0Km5CJX5yE4zXu2/Zke5l9pThhXDkhv6JxFFKZpvfAgY6DQ0\nF2mylEDSiPFba3vJ7ngSSCxb25BE2krEewkvG5HwuS+Vb9jjj1i66I9CcRZ8eKfV\nZPky4e0v8+xQjHejceK2J+A9Fdo7VMUDv9beIG/g2ML0lBZdIODhh3+udkj545ll\nstWq6LJLOdIHAbWonzRe2XdnCz03IlMvQY1Aep4uf/3T/rH9XmUGAacd