ken/signalk-container-helper/commit/90d1356afd0caf7cf66a2e45fe2a957bb38bfa1a","sha":"90d1356afd0caf7cf66a2e45fe2a957bb38bfa1a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hoeken/signalk-container-helper/commits/90d1356afd0caf7cf66a2e45fe2a957bb38bfa1a"}],"sha":"aee9aace42d470bfbfa9124d8d7d826e4621c1bc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hoeken/signalk-container-helper/commits/aee9aace42d470bfbfa9124d8d7d826e4621c1bc"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/86628605?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dirkwa","id":86628605,"login":"dirkwa","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg2NjI4NjA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hoeken/signalk-container-helper/commits/90d1356afd0caf7cf66a2e45fe2a957bb38bfa1a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-22T21:11:20Z","email":"86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Dirk Wahrheit"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-22T21:11:20Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: expose probeHostDevice and mirror VolumeSpec.readOnly (#43)\n\n* feat: expose probeHostDevice and mirror VolumeSpec.readOnly\n\nA plugin cannot tell whether the host has a device: stat''ing answers for\nthe plugin''s own filesystem, which is the Signal K container in the common\ndeployment, and that container has no /dev/dri even on a machine with a\nGPU. signalk-container can see the host, so this wraps its new probe the\nsame way resolveMount wraps resolveHostPath — takes the manager, validates\nthe path, and throws a typed unsupported-manager error on an older\nsignalk-container so a plugin degrades instead of crashing.\n\nnull means \"unknown\" and is deliberately distinct from {exists: false},\nwhich means \"definitely absent\". Callers must not collapse the two.\n\nGroups come back as NAMES because that is what groupAdd wants: the gid of\nrender or video differs per distro, so a hardcoded number silently loses\naccess elsewhere.\n\nAlso mirrors VolumeSpec.readOnly, so a plugin can share a directory\nanother component owns without granting write access to it.\n\nNote: test/types-contract.test-d.ts fails on master already — the pinned\nsignalk-container devDependency (1.25.5) predates types the contract\nexpects. Unrelated to this change; the runtime suite is green at 161.\n\n* docs: document probeHostDevice and readOnly volumes\n\n* docs: restore the docblock this branch orphaned\n\nInserting probeHostDevice between resolveHostPath''s docblock and its\nsignature left resolveHostPath undocumented and gave probeHostDevice two\ncomments. Each method carries its own again, and probeHostDevice''s now\nexplains why a plugin cannot answer the question itself rather than\npointing at the helper for it.\n\n* refactor: drop a redundant re-export\n\nhost-device.ts re-exported the same HostDeviceProbeResult it imports from\ntypes.ts, which index.ts already exports wholesale — two paths to one\ntype on the public surface for no benefit. Verified with a consumer-shaped\ntypecheck that both the function and the type still resolve from the\npackage root.","tree":{"sha":"d5aa26b85f60b842642296dabf6cd887b1a02286","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hoeken/signalk-container-helper/git/trees/d5aa26b85f60b842642296dabf6cd887b1a02286"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hoeken/signalk-container-helper/git/commits/90d1356afd0caf7cf66a2e45fe2a957bb38bfa1a","verification":{"payload":"tree d5aa26b85f60b842642296dabf6cd887b1a02286\nparent 932cce5ac7d2f6f148ea44bbbaefa1ecc806ed33\nauthor Dirk Wahrheit <86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com> 1787433080 +1200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787433080 +1200\n\nfeat: expose probeHostDevice and mirror VolumeSpec.readOnly (#43)\n\n* feat: expose probeHostDevice and mirror VolumeSpec.readOnly\n\nA plugin cannot tell whether the host has a device: stat''ing answers for\nthe plugin''s own filesystem, which is the Signal K container in the common\ndeployment, and that container has no /dev/dri even on a machine with a\nGPU. signalk-container can see the host, so this wraps its new probe the\nsame way resolveMount wraps resolveHostPath — takes the manager, validates\nthe path, and throws a typed unsupported-manager error on an older\nsignalk-container so a plugin degrades instead of crashing.\n\nnull means \"unknown\" and is deliberately distinct from {exists: false},\nwhich means \"definitely absent\". Callers must not collapse the two.\n\nGroups come back as NAMES because that is what groupAdd wants: the gid of\nrender or video differs per distro, so a hardcoded number silently loses\naccess elsewhere.\n\nAlso mirrors VolumeSpec.readOnly, so a plugin can share a directory\nanother component owns without granting write access to it.\n\nNote: test/types-contract.test-d.ts fails on master already — the pinned\nsignalk-container devDependency (1.25.5) predates types the contract\nexpects. Unrelated to this change; the runtime suite is green at 161.\n\n* docs: document probeHostDevice and readOnly volumes\n\n* docs: restore the docblock this branch orphaned\n\nInserting probeHostDevice between resolveHostPath''s docblock and its\nsignature left resolveHostPath undocumented and gave probeHostDevice two\ncomments. Each method carries its own again, and probeHostDevice''s now\nexplains why a plugin cannot answer the question itself rather than\npointing at the helper for it.\n\n* refactor: drop a redundant re-export\n\nhost-device.ts re-exported the same HostDeviceProbeResult it imports from\ntypes.ts, which index.ts already exports wholesale — two paths to one\ntype on the public surface for no benefit. Verified with a consumer-shaped\ntypecheck that both the function and the type still resolve from the\npackage root.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqihB4CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAHSMQAIEg8+8UC/gH6Aao13gl9Be9\nH60cknJVGdyjX0kaBq/MYZG/m6LD5qjY1l8yiwlyYXXvOYEdnsBRXAwFZo4+hdCt\nmwTM+QFEw0SEcXCAfiSuyUtXavIP88Rp9eEKMQROA9BCEIOwb2aie+I4Wh43vGUw\n49XieE6Qm3w0pGjEyMa0rIBEPccAuFcGoiW0ndJwN8TwNjzj7m3IZCE1QlrXUi1m\nkoPnqyVHAEqUA3erUjQz43EA7bdHDNYH3wR4FijSd0cPGcWsE7YSNkSDH6j5/mCK\nJkjdEqIeff7jyFlljl60as7v/Cm9FFIE10c3MSd9EIpIUARNgbuKatyM42ZPUZwy\nT2B6HZ70xh+kqh2K6+B2UHRQQ5BI1gBcPP/GeLMU3ejEYyWG/c45jjMR1B7BLJQE\n6GXz7uIxIZ5UTtbZUVnux7KIWFYSstPwLksbcJYe86+CPg35jOEWsICFmLEtGDon\nZ2kIPySueWpjfAh8j/WLd0jMsTFP99O5UXkSZl6Lu/8ZKBmzOKOtnnaPbRUxAG+G\nc4l2R90JRyz6tc/2/y17mL6xXKN8ZyECYTd0aPJvrebxCcbX2DDuWgdeVOjQyEE1\nzBhCPYeZnhtZEhEwhgjiZyHNtDkjU8iU4xMgs0oCewUNX0W0knPeD/zSCKjIntRS\nbkM/H8zFNphSIl0sDjCb\n=fhd8\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-22T21:11:21Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/hoeken/signalk-container-helper/commit/90d1356afd0caf7cf66a2e45fe2a957bb38bfa1a","node_id":"C_kwDOTgx649oAKDkwZDEzNTZhZmQwY2FmN2NmNjZhMmU0NWZlMmE5NTdiYjM4YmZhMWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/hoeken/signalk-container-helper/commit/932cce5ac7d2f6f148ea44bbbaefa1ecc806ed33","sha":"932cce5ac7d2f6f148ea44bbbaefa1ecc806ed33","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hoeken/signalk-container-helper/commits/932cce5ac7d2f6f148ea44bbbaefa1ecc806ed33"}],"sha":"90d1356afd0caf7cf66a2e45fe2a957bb38bfa1a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hoeken/signalk-container-helper/commits/90d1356afd0caf7cf66a2e45fe2a957bb38bfa1a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/86628605?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dirkwa","id":86628605,"login":"dirkwa","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg2NjI4NjA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hoeken/signalk-container-helper/commits/932cce5ac7d2f6f148ea44bbbaefa1ecc806ed33/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-22T21:11:04Z","email":"86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Dirk Wahrheit"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-22T21:11:04Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: add a managed/self-hosted endpoint switch (#44)\n\n* feat: add a managed/self-hosted endpoint switch\n\nOperators who already run a service elsewhere — on a NAS, another Pi, or a\nbox that is doing the job anyway — want to point a plugin at it instead of\nhaving signalk-container run a container for it. Several plugins offer this\nalready, and each wrote its own: the empty-URL guard string is duplicated\nverbatim in two of them, and the manager lookup is reimplemented in four.\n\nresolveEndpoint() yields a base URL for either mode, so the transport half\nof a consumer stops caring which mode it is in. Three details are load-bearing:\n\n- `undefined` means managed. Signal K calls start() with {} when a plugin is\n  enabled without its form ever being saved, so Boolean(managedContainer)\n  would flip exactly those installs into self-hosted mode with an empty URL.\n  isManagedMode() names that rule for the route guards that only need the\n  mode question.\n- Readiness retries are opt-in. The reference plugins genuinely differ —\n  one retries forever because an unattended boat must heal itself, another\n  reports once and waits — so imposing either would change behaviour under\n  cover of a refactor.\n- managedModeSchema() emits plain JSON Schema. Consumers are split between\n  typebox 1.x and @sinclair/typebox 0.34, which are mutually incompatible,\n  and this library depends on neither. Splice with Type.Unsafe: a bare\n  fragment compiles under typebox 1.x and fails under 0.34.\n\nScope: \"self-hosted\" means the service runs elsewhere, never a container\nengine elsewhere — signalk-container drives local unix sockets only and\nrejects a tcp:// endpoint.\n\nsrc/url.ts uses the URL global, not node:url: it is imported by both the\nNode and browser entries, and the main entry imports no Node builtins.\n\n* fix: keep an explicitly typed scheme-default port\n\n`URL` discards a port that matches the scheme default, so `url.port` reads\n\"\" for both \"http://nas.local\" and \"http://nas.local:80\". Applying\ndefaultPort on that alone moved an operator who deliberately typed :80 (or\n:443) onto the plugin''s own port instead — silently, and only in the\nself-hosted path where the address is the whole point.\n\nInspect the authority the operator actually wrote, before URL normalises it.\nThe check skips the colons inside a bracketed IPv6 literal, so \"[::1]\" still\ntakes defaultPort while \"[::1]:80\" keeps its port.\n\n* test: pin that credentials in a URL are not read as a port\n\n* docs: say why the schema fragment is plain JSON Schema\n\nThe obvious reaction to \"two incompatible TypeBox packages\" is to lift every\nplugin onto typebox 1.x and drop the accommodation. That does not work:\n@signalk/server-api depends on @sinclair/typebox 0.34 itself, so the scoped\npackage is in every consumer''s tree whichever one the plugin picks for its\nown schema — signalk-questdb already resolves both. Migrating adds a second\nTypeBox beside the first rather than replacing it.\n\nRecord that, and the case for migrating anyway on its own merits: the scoped\npackage is frozen at 0.34.52, and for the constructs these plugins use the\ntwo emit semantically identical JSON Schema, so it is an import swap rather\nthan a port.\n\nAlso corrects an overstatement: Type.Unsafe and Type.Boolean emit the same\nkeys and values in a different ORDER, so \"byte-identical\" was wrong. Key\norder is meaningless to JSON Schema and RJSF, but an assertion comparing\nstrings while migrating a plugin would fail on it.\n\n* fix: reject hostnames WHATWG URL waves through\n\nSelf-audit findings, none of which the existing tests caught.\n\n`new URL(''\"http://x:3010'')` does not throw — it parses with hostname `\"http`,\nso a mangled paste produced a baseUrl of `http://\"http` that was handed to\nfetch and written to the plugin log. WHATWG URL also tolerates backticks and\nbraces in a hostname. Guard the hostname against what a name or IP literal\ncan legally contain; unicode has already been punycoded by that point, so\ncafé.local still works.\n\nRelated: only strip wrapping quotes when they are BALANCED. An unbalanced one\nis not a paste artefact to tidy away, it is input the operator needs told\nabout — and it was the vector for the above.\n\nAlso report an explicitly typed scheme-default port. URL() drops :80 and :443\nas scheme defaults, so `http://x:80` yielded port null. baseUrl is unaffected\neither way, but a consumer reading `.port` for a non-HTTP protocol — a raw TCP\ningest port, say — got null for a port the operator stated outright. This is\nthe same class of bug CodeRabbit caught on the defaultPort path; that fix\naddressed only half of it.\n\nCorrects a stale doc comment on ResolvedEndpoint.address, and uses the\ncaller''s placeholder in the panel''s validation hint rather than hardcoding an\nexample that may not match the product.\n\n* fix: validate defaultPort and correct two stale descriptions\n\nThree review findings on the audit commit, all valid.\n\n`options.defaultPort` was never range-checked, though a port parsed out of\nthe URL was — so a caller mistake produced addresses like `http://x:NaN`.\nBoth paths now share one predicate.\n\nThe `port` doc comment still said null meant \"the URL relies on the scheme''s\ndefault port\". That stopped being true in the previous commit, which made an\nexplicitly typed :80 report as 80; null now means no port was typed and none\nwas defaulted.\n\nmanagedModeSchema''s description said \"When enabled (default)\" even when\ndefaultManaged was false, telling the operator the opposite of the truth.","tree":{"sha":"e613e3f6de280a3381aada69821e13d08b30bbad","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hoeken/signalk-container-helper/git/trees/e613e3f6de280a3381aada69821e13d08b30bbad"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hoeken/signalk-container-helper/git/commits/932cce5ac7d2f6f148ea44bbbaefa1ecc806ed33","verification":{"payload":"tree e613e3f6de280a3381aada69821e13d08b30bbad\nparent 75543d07bbeed92a8124257ef955ba7caad1af67\nauthor Dirk Wahrheit <86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com> 1787433064 +1200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787433064 +1200\n\nfeat: add a managed/self-hosted endpoint switch (#44)\n\n* feat: add a managed/self-hosted endpoint switch\n\nOperators who already run a service elsewhere — on a NAS, another Pi, or a\nbox that is doing the job anyway — want to point a plugin at it instead of\nhaving signalk-container run a container for it. Several plugins offer this\nalready, and each wrote its own: the empty-URL guard string is duplicated\nverbatim in two of them, and the manager lookup is reimplemented in four.\n\nresolveEndpoint() yields a base URL for either mode, so the transport half\nof a consumer stops caring which mode it is in. Three details are load-bearing:\n\n- `undefined` means managed. Signal K calls start() with {} when a plugin is\n  enabled without its form ever being saved, so Boolean(managedContainer)\n  would flip exactly those installs into self-hosted mode with an empty URL.\n  isManagedMode() names that rule for the route guards that only need the\n  mode question.\n- Readiness retries are opt-in. The reference plugins genuinely differ —\n  one retries forever because an unattended boat must heal itself, another\n  reports once and waits — so imposing either would change behaviour under\n  cover of a refactor.\n- managedModeSchema() emits plain JSON Schema. Consumers are split between\n  typebox 1.x and @sinclair/typebox 0.34, which are mutually incompatible,\n  and this library depends on neither. Splice with Type.Unsafe: a bare\n  fragment compiles under typebox 1.x and fails under 0.34.\n\nScope: \"self-hosted\" means the service runs elsewhere, never a container\nengine elsewhere — signalk-container drives local unix sockets only and\nrejects a tcp:// endpoint.\n\nsrc/url.ts uses the URL global, not node:url: it is imported by both the\nNode and browser entries, and the main entry imports no Node builtins.\n\n* fix: keep an explicitly typed scheme-default port\n\n`URL` discards a port that matches the scheme default, so `url.port` reads\n\"\" for both \"http://nas.local\" and \"http://nas.local:80\". Applying\ndefaultPort on that alone moved an operator who deliberately typed :80 (or\n:443) onto the plugin''s own port instead — silently, and only in the\nself-hosted path where the address is the whole point.\n\nInspect the authority the operator actually wrote, before URL normalises it.\nThe check skips the colons inside a bracketed IPv6 literal, so \"[::1]\" still\ntakes defaultPort while \"[::1]:80\" keeps its port.\n\n* test: pin that credentials in a URL are not read as a port\n\n* docs: say why the schema fragment is plain JSON Schema\n\nThe obvious reaction to \"two incompatible TypeBox packages\" is to lift every\nplugin onto typebox 1.x and drop the accommodation. That does not work:\n@signalk/server-api depends on @sinclair/typebox 0.34 itself, so the scoped\npackage is in every consumer''s tree whichever one the plugin picks for its\nown schema — signalk-questdb already resolves both. Migrating adds a second\nTypeBox beside the first rather than replacing it.\n\nRecord that, and the case for migrating anyway on its own merits: the scoped\npackage is frozen at 0.34.52, and for the constructs these plugins use the\ntwo emit semantically identical JSON Schema, so it is an import swap rather\nthan a port.\n\nAlso corrects an overstatement: Type.Unsafe and Type.Boolean emit the same\nkeys and values in a different ORDER, so \"byte-identical\" was wrong. Key\norder is meaningless to JSON Schema and RJSF, but an assertion comparing\nstrings while migrating a plugin would fail on it.\n\n* fix: reject hostnames WHATWG URL waves through\n\nSelf-audit findings, none of which the existing tests caught.\n\n`new URL(''\"http://x:3010'')` does not throw — it parses with hostname `\"http`,\nso a mangled paste produced a baseUrl of `http://\"http` that was handed to\nfetch and written to the plugin log. WHATWG URL also tolerates backticks and\nbraces in a hostname. Guard the hostname against what a name or IP literal\ncan legally contain; unicode has already been punycoded by that point, so\ncafé.local still works.\n\nRelated: only strip wrapping quotes when they are BALANCED. An unbalanced one\nis not a paste artefact to tidy away, it is input the operator needs told\nabout — and it was the vector for the above.\n\nAlso report an explicitly typed scheme-default port. URL() drops :80 and :443\nas scheme defaults, so `http://x:80` yielded port null. baseUrl is unaffected\neither way, but a consumer reading `.port` for a non-HTTP protocol — a raw TCP\ningest port, say — got null for a port the operator stated outright. This is\nthe same class of bug CodeRabbit caught on the defaultPort path; that fix\naddressed only half of it.\n\nCorrects a stale doc comment on ResolvedEndpoint.address, and uses the\ncaller''s placeholder in the panel''s validation hint rather than hardcoding an\nexample that may not match the product.\n\n* fix: validate defaultPort and correct two stale descriptions\n\nThree review findings on the audit commit, all valid.\n\n`options.defaultPort` was never range-checked, though a port parsed out of\nthe URL was — so a caller mistake produced addresses like `http://x:NaN`.\nBoth paths now share one predicate.\n\nThe `port` doc comment still said null meant \"the URL relies on the scheme''s\ndefault port\". That stopped being true in the previous commit, which made an\nexplicitly typed :80 report as 80; null now means no port was typed and none\nwas defaulted.\n\nmanagedModeSchema''s description said \"When enabled (default)\" even when\ndefaultManaged was false, telling the operator the opposite of the truth.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqihBoCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAYGwQAIo4K8xLKfHKPv78EHmVFHbo\nJMcgZHrYTB3KBPa9i7SBL8yoLv7MlmLICUiVswW9OMHJ0q4GcsA1j7K5hdlsUqCF\nelDOzUWGMSBefpmJzZU05pSlshVKvEuuBJ0YxwRSBETFj7pcTXy9Gq965jgRMs41\nN5P3avWvfXnOU0Va61ZVx1r6tnm3E+Jg5cqL92gQDxJ/ax1Yn7CgoTIW6w19D9a6\ntHLSIt2U/h7RELpq8qMY6JNAGcoUAC4h7wkc1OfipTyd1PHovf+AVKDQz2q3AgEs\nyw6aA0HiHXhFiWJOAFyT9yaGchNluyMj40FWiqFbFHiicTsKtIlp7QhEzNHGNjwu\n9kib9PwcPsfS7RQ6cxBHNoplpV+gGy/Ebi/Y8o+4qLrGKxrMtoVcDOxWSahejrGP\nTLjii3iTMA97PVxyVxtDlGL9nOxBC+oRUfCpDKUHGEKYuR1oyYlqx+squRAfZVS8\n/mmE9K3LP9mmRWOyJqTg6uA0clUuZAAMLmWkDhknuEuSDhXF/b0kLnu2znF+vKI6\nJ9uXl4bny78wq/aCvdixPZbZGgC7TEd77EO+LFIARrduJJzROjeITg6TVYnElWq4\ncUQwCQ7Ojr1IC1vQxgnM3+v/6I7hfme36T4IDKnmlKY8La0j3vW8p61r2N/T1mug\nwhYjG7cG1F4VWJ9W/tvG\n=aCFX\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-22T21:11:05Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/hoeken/signalk-container-helper/commit/932cce5ac7d2f6f148ea44bbbaefa1ecc806ed33","node_id":"C_kwDOTgx649oAKDkzMmNjZTVhYzdkMmY2ZjE0OGVhNDRiYmJhZWZhMWVjYzgwNmVkMzM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/hoeken/signalk-container-helper/commit/75543d07bbeed92a8124257ef955ba7caad1af67","sha":"75543d07bbeed92a8124257ef955ba7caad1af67","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hoeken/signalk-container-helper/commits/75543d07bbeed92a8124257ef955ba7caad1af67"}],"sha":"932cce5ac7d2f6f148ea44bbbaefa1ecc806ed33","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hoeken/signalk-container-helper/commits/932cce5ac7d2f6f148ea44bbbaefa1ecc806ed33"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/86628605?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dirkwa","id":86628605,"login":"dirkwa","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg2NjI4NjA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hoeken/signalk-container-helper/commits/75543d07bbeed92a8124257ef955ba7caad1af67/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-18T21:54:50Z","email":"86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Dirk Wahrheit"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-18T21:54:50Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore(release): 0.7.0 (#41)","tree":{"sha":"045179a49daee00583cbf44cd59c3dfe9dcf941a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hoeken/signa