n\nCo-authored-by: dirkwa <dirkwahrtheit@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqe0xjCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAjPAQAFGOiSodOkY8Ox7NriwYUm2O\nSuzuDPo9JK12aOFXQdFfZUAFO2V9L2fBNfDBEmKDLCMFSXlTQ4Hyl7xwPz9E3ptL\n1R3xQbdOaHi4OkxtfClCaFOFEFXE3WwnuTI6E8IRxDEsGFd6CJUp3H6yiuJsJkR6\neXHLbHQY9n68F8rHtAO4PIHARr5GKCO1BAMfDd00iPlU34MA4DaK5wuD1QN06yEA\ncpcA7XKfYlbMD7ojddRpmevHjO/b4/aAWFyqmxXlZqabDP72IOE94ctSxJH3GYJA\nmxHhvcLduOJkwdCPEYlHJP1N8cPL9Q2iD8AC3ki16ECjl7gKpdarTHy0+A59pQ6m\n/NtNxEPS581Lnt7+kEpilMrdPSaFPdl+JxTQloHCsAUDNvlZTSolx0wsXprgt9IG\nh6y11NjL8d3ODC7zZ5hf3FSP8KmGZk83hPkYjDPfuSF4i+HjjlF7WtNpL2Te4BoK\n0uAH8Fmym73nRNXwyMzorzb2BlZwv7sasJHi3M1f9VAwqNBBfwhMUd0slZRUCqcM\nqR0V/pq6IvQrpIKHmxD3oGnx/XydZC7nYMV/DjQFV1G5JgdZnuLMxFkHrjfBNjnv\nkdojaUj7d8hhmPJSjKMAT2cWf6ABHO49pRmco6WKwDKe8JcKkK21DnPNQmpcrIls\n8laSCPk9IAU0OkkWr9rR\n=e9kM\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-11T16:28:58Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/hoeken/signalk-container-helper/commit/ccdebcd005b1803eb6ca25c8df032315eca5599d","node_id":"C_kwDOTgx649oAKGNjZGViY2QwMDViMTgwM2ViNmNhMjVjOGRmMDMyMzE1ZWNhNTU5OWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/hoeken/signalk-container-helper/commit/7c61d1f0baacc240588b425880aa514ba048f482","sha":"7c61d1f0baacc240588b425880aa514ba048f482","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hoeken/signalk-container-helper/commits/7c61d1f0baacc240588b425880aa514ba048f482"}],"sha":"ccdebcd005b1803eb6ca25c8df032315eca5599d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hoeken/signalk-container-helper/commits/ccdebcd005b1803eb6ca25c8df032315eca5599d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/86628605?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dirkwa","id":86628605,"login":"dirkwa","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg2NjI4NjA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hoeken/signalk-container-helper/commits/7c61d1f0baacc240588b425880aa514ba048f482/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-11T16:13:31Z","email":"86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Dirk Wahrheit"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-11T16:13:31Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(types): correct signalkDataMount semantics, add resolveMount (#36)\n\n* fix(types): document signalkDataMount as signalk-container''s own data dir\n\nsrc/types.ts is a documented mirror of signalk-container''s API, and this\nfield''s JSDoc had drifted semantically from its source. Upstream says a\nconsumer plugin asking for signalkDataMount \"gets only the signalk-container\nplugin''s own state subdirectory\"; our copy said \"the plugin''s Signal K data\ndir\". Same words, inverted meaning -- in the manager''s file \"the plugin\" is\nsignalk-container itself, while every line around ours addresses a consumer\nplugin author.\n\nThe contract test cannot catch this: it asserts structure and name coverage,\nnot JSDoc, so the mirror stayed green while telling consumers the opposite of\nthe truth. Reported as issue #35 by a user who read the docs correctly.\n\nThe README compounded it by putting \"// plugin data dir\" directly under\npluginId: \"signalk-myservice\". Drop that line from the quick start rather\nthan correcting it in place -- keeping it there still models the wrong thing\nfor the common case -- and add a section covering the three-way choice\nbetween signalkDataMount, signalkConfigRootMount, and resolving your own\ndata dir, including the named-volume subPath trap.\n\n* feat(host-path): add resolveMount for consumer-owned directories\n\nMounting your own plugin''s data directory had no supported path. Issue #35\nshows the two ways consumers get it wrong: signalkDataMount resolves to\nsignalk-container''s own dir, and passing app.getDataDirPath() straight into\nvolumes works bare-metal but fails once Signal K is containerized, because\nthe host daemon cannot see a path that only exists inside the SK container.\n\nThe manager already ships resolveHostPath for this, and signalk-questdb\nhand-wrote the wrapper around it. Package that here so the next consumer\ndoes not: feature-detect the method, translate the path, and turn both\nfailure modes into typed errors.\n\nThe subtle part is subPath, which is why this is worth a helper rather than\na doc snippet. Runtimes reject `-v volume/sub:/dest`, so when Signal K''s\ndata dir lives on a named volume the resolver returns the volume as the\nsource plus an offset; bind mounts return an empty offset because the host\npath is bound directly. A consumer who ignores it works on bare-metal and\nbind-mounted Docker, then silently reads the volume root instead of its own\ndirectory. HostMount.containerPath has the offset joined already.\n\nAn unreachable path throws rather than falling back to the untranslated\npath: falling back reproduces the `statfs: no such file or directory`\nfailure the manager''s guide warns about, just later and less clearly.\n\nTakes hostPath as a string rather than reading app.getDataDirPath() itself,\nso \"which plugin''s data dir?\" -- the confusion behind #35 -- has to be\nanswered explicitly at the call site. Standalone function rather than a\nManagedContainer option because buildConfig is synchronous; an option would\nforce a breaking async signature or hidden config mutation, and the tests\nnow pin that pass-through invariant.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: dirkwa <dirkwahrtheit@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"a798efd938a0070f001d49aa4476451e088e1358","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hoeken/signalk-container-helper/git/trees/a798efd938a0070f001d49aa4476451e088e1358"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hoeken/signalk-container-helper/git/commits/7c61d1f0baacc240588b425880aa514ba048f482","verification":{"payload":"tree a798efd938a0070f001d49aa4476451e088e1358\nparent 8dfa6269643509932b4c00f0b9e2c6802d25ff48\nauthor Dirk Wahrheit <86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com> 1786464811 +1200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786464811 +1200\n\nfix(types): correct signalkDataMount semantics, add resolveMount (#36)\n\n* fix(types): document signalkDataMount as signalk-container''s own data dir\n\nsrc/types.ts is a documented mirror of signalk-container''s API, and this\nfield''s JSDoc had drifted semantically from its source. Upstream says a\nconsumer plugin asking for signalkDataMount \"gets only the signalk-container\nplugin''s own state subdirectory\"; our copy said \"the plugin''s Signal K data\ndir\". Same words, inverted meaning -- in the manager''s file \"the plugin\" is\nsignalk-container itself, while every line around ours addresses a consumer\nplugin author.\n\nThe contract test cannot catch this: it asserts structure and name coverage,\nnot JSDoc, so the mirror stayed green while telling consumers the opposite of\nthe truth. Reported as issue #35 by a user who read the docs correctly.\n\nThe README compounded it by putting \"// plugin data dir\" directly under\npluginId: \"signalk-myservice\". Drop that line from the quick start rather\nthan correcting it in place -- keeping it there still models the wrong thing\nfor the common case -- and add a section covering the three-way choice\nbetween signalkDataMount, signalkConfigRootMount, and resolving your own\ndata dir, including the named-volume subPath trap.\n\n* feat(host-path): add resolveMount for consumer-owned directories\n\nMounting your own plugin''s data directory had no supported path. Issue #35\nshows the two ways consumers get it wrong: signalkDataMount resolves to\nsignalk-container''s own dir, and passing app.getDataDirPath() straight into\nvolumes works bare-metal but fails once Signal K is containerized, because\nthe host daemon cannot see a path that only exists inside the SK container.\n\nThe manager already ships resolveHostPath for this, and signalk-questdb\nhand-wrote the wrapper around it. Package that here so the next consumer\ndoes not: feature-detect the method, translate the path, and turn both\nfailure modes into typed errors.\n\nThe subtle part is subPath, which is why this is worth a helper rather than\na doc snippet. Runtimes reject `-v volume/sub:/dest`, so when Signal K''s\ndata dir lives on a named volume the resolver returns the volume as the\nsource plus an offset; bind mounts return an empty offset because the host\npath is bound directly. A consumer who ignores it works on bare-metal and\nbind-mounted Docker, then silently reads the volume root instead of its own\ndirectory. HostMount.containerPath has the offset joined already.\n\nAn unreachable path throws rather than falling back to the untranslated\npath: falling back reproduces the `statfs: no such file or directory`\nfailure the manager''s guide warns about, just later and less clearly.\n\nTakes hostPath as a string rather than reading app.getDataDirPath() itself,\nso \"which plugin''s data dir?\" -- the confusion behind #35 -- has to be\nanswered explicitly at the call site. Standalone function rather than a\nManagedContainer option because buildConfig is synchronous; an option would\nforce a breaking async signature or hidden config mutation, and the tests\nnow pin that pass-through invariant.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: dirkwa <dirkwahrtheit@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqe0orCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAsmYQAABeICMpEW9e6TnZm8+wJybN\nlDHmkUHmbjik0J/HPHp1CUd3kA/YB1qrCmhSaZnW/t0UuoMRekpa6JPkzHxxYoAn\nz5g74oJsepevMTjiqaEOzzDBMXOJeO7MLMhLfGGrUMZOaKFWbOi1hlbr21LJyN23\nSwK2yJmh1WpEqfSlKuLOe2gcxfFV0rstVoCn/55D1Eg9RExncIoYWAkY+MzLrjqt\nxXGsAnJFNku4lAnzAjLCVew6ggn3lmYCyJPLjbaRvmbe5DXtglbp7wvKqm+8N8rx\nZ5ETmtKtnRGZQF/zlTh9ZKcp6Sv3cagKP57c/znGGfqoxPXD3YH0KHWURZlMc8LD\n5Ii1WIkq2EcVaYF79N3CCplnKbpGxxAVyCnmo6T4ErTmcvbLpapeJHWmkXeb6hnR\nkJDjMX+1RiDriN0kARaejvG1H4ol2E4LGtjS2tGzcadA2lu8vG4nJUtpuLAzijw+\n+O32+c52GUFo2OxOhVrO6lUZFyShxxG2Ygy15erUCAwkn7vxoin0tZIkG9sAg2gf\n+LVJwIe+/NcV0Schp4XkmMQI7X7QD78ZM7gAwtx+YY6oZLm1M4eWyFQ8u4R1ZdXp\nXElDaupq2OrJWpfHTDr2bbDrmpBeD1S91MBDCO+YKeU4H1WF78XDGRR215Dzmiqq\n/qqEXWLPutrOsVA++pSJ\n=ZLbs\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-11T16:13:34Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/hoeken/signalk-container-helper/commit/7c61d1f0baacc240588b425880aa514ba048f482","node_id":"C_kwDOTgx649oAKDdjNjFkMWYwYmFhY2MyNDA1ODhiNDI1ODgwYWE1MTRiYTA0OGY0ODI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/hoeken/signalk-container-helper/commit/8dfa6269643509932b4c00f0b9e2c6802d25ff48","sha":"8dfa6269643509932b4c00f0b9e2c6802d25ff48","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hoeken/signalk-container-helper/commits/8dfa6269643509932b4c00f0b9e2c6802d25ff48"}],"sha":"7c61d1f0baacc240588b425880aa514ba048f482","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hoeken/signalk-container-helper/commits/7c61d1f0baacc240588b425880aa514ba048f482"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/86628605?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dirkwa","id":86628605,"login":"dirkwa","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg2NjI4NjA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/received_events","rep