rl":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dirkwa","id":86628605,"login":"dirkwa","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg2NjI4NjA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hoeken/signalk-container-helper/commits/b9d6911b8b215d113d0ef0c8ea8ef145478d8b7a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-10T22:37:50Z","email":"86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Dirk Wahrheit"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-10T22:37:50Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore: drop CHANGELOG.md in favour of generated release notes (#33)\n\nThe hand-maintained changelog duplicated what the git history already records,\nand publish.yml parsed it by exact heading — a missing or misspelled\n`# vX.Y.Z` section was a hard failure of the release job, so the file was a\nrelease-time trap as well as a maintenance cost.\n\nRelease notes now come from GitHub''s own generation over the PRs merged since\nthe previous tag, grouped into sections by .github/release.yml (the pattern\nsignalk-container already uses). The release job checks out with\nfetch-depth: 0, which note generation needs to diff against the previous tag.\n\nThis puts real weight on PR titles: they are the release notes a consumer\nreads, not just merge subjects. AGENTS.md now says so explicitly and requires\nAngular style for both commit subjects and PR titles, and notes that an\nunlabelled PR falls through to the \"Other\" section.\n\nAlso gitignores cr-review* — local coderabbit CLI output, regenerated per run\nand never meant to be committed.\n\nCo-authored-by: dirkwa <dirkwahrtheit@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"a140b37b0e4bc56c23955f5da45a4fedf0169b24","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hoeken/signalk-container-helper/git/trees/a140b37b0e4bc56c23955f5da45a4fedf0169b24"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hoeken/signalk-container-helper/git/commits/b9d6911b8b215d113d0ef0c8ea8ef145478d8b7a","verification":{"payload":"tree a140b37b0e4bc56c23955f5da45a4fedf0169b24\nparent 37c782613b8899e31818081c23b95c7f7402d18c\nauthor Dirk Wahrheit <86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com> 1786401470 +1200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786401470 +1200\n\nchore: drop CHANGELOG.md in favour of generated release notes (#33)\n\nThe hand-maintained changelog duplicated what the git history already records,\nand publish.yml parsed it by exact heading — a missing or misspelled\n`# vX.Y.Z` section was a hard failure of the release job, so the file was a\nrelease-time trap as well as a maintenance cost.\n\nRelease notes now come from GitHub''s own generation over the PRs merged since\nthe previous tag, grouped into sections by .github/release.yml (the pattern\nsignalk-container already uses). The release job checks out with\nfetch-depth: 0, which note generation needs to diff against the previous tag.\n\nThis puts real weight on PR titles: they are the release notes a consumer\nreads, not just merge subjects. AGENTS.md now says so explicitly and requires\nAngular style for both commit subjects and PR titles, and notes that an\nunlabelled PR falls through to the \"Other\" section.\n\nAlso gitignores cr-review* — local coderabbit CLI output, regenerated per run\nand never meant to be committed.\n\nCo-authored-by: dirkwa <dirkwahrtheit@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqelK+CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAPbEQAFK6Yg5jp71E0NNvrpdkaXUL\nehu6DXhTZi87OvYmb6nDjIAKqZW9Dr7SIwQyE63v3KsVF5aYHeiX4+s+9FU8cy3A\nNm3wAglJlfLkMvEQohFm64L1OJwZsIz7VZ0bkoTOk44ccDYpSlmaDCPSS/slBYJ1\nJHUyRubpr3MvSekt8WPaGyt/0WDcl83NO5o6Xp1Jn3U+eQW70vM9Gevy3oKy8tsk\nYUhdhNLAx0EoDUK5GpagsEvD3IAj6vdwhbWF/aoRYtH78BMAqTyCfaAdOYgltztT\nA0hsrBKwgxzStVwgtiA/SSjEoPLGIhH+Y8BdvL5pOgt0Zf9RfzMeO+xLFOf2eUFo\nFR8M6VgQMWVZwD2YEYEr7jYpFj7lai6/ZTRswyKYpZd/Wdp6DQeb5zxQF9DSHQMi\nCwBg/88c5+ANlqUUceZw7eo1rooUB7ZAYWP0woj2yxuxDhqjP+rrgKCNeKGcB9pL\nXue87m6zrIED2LLOtJN6s5RRtIhVJfeesGoOkIOeoqTl1DyIl3ziGvoM7NsmqLYY\nbdFeAGGafTiDfHp0kWnPbQa6hTqO8VAu5fnZQSYblnYa5e2vlRt2hiAMD9BSn5Qm\nGoPfPsfJahsMzIRC6oNMvbbztrcKDXoWn9LZEgAvEXAQa2N8Fvd+DfVDRx7yaRa1\nUWbkp3p8yPP2hXV/S4jJ\n=UAtQ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-10T22:37:55Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/hoeken/signalk-container-helper/commit/b9d6911b8b215d113d0ef0c8ea8ef145478d8b7a","node_id":"C_kwDOTgx649oAKGI5ZDY5MTFiOGIyMTVkMTEzZDBlZjBjOGVhOGVmMTQ1NDc4ZDhiN2E","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/hoeken/signalk-container-helper/commit/37c782613b8899e31818081c23b95c7f7402d18c","sha":"37c782613b8899e31818081c23b95c7f7402d18c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hoeken/signalk-container-helper/commits/37c782613b8899e31818081c23b95c7f7402d18c"}],"sha":"b9d6911b8b215d113d0ef0c8ea8ef145478d8b7a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hoeken/signalk-container-helper/commits/b9d6911b8b215d113d0ef0c8ea8ef145478d8b7a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/86628605?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dirkwa","id":86628605,"login":"dirkwa","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg2NjI4NjA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hoeken/signalk-container-helper/commits/37c782613b8899e31818081c23b95c7f7402d18c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-10T22:33:43Z","email":"86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Dirk Wahrheit"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-10T22:33:43Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(retry): add retryForever and ManagedContainer readinessRetry (#32)\n\nstart() throws once when bring-up fails, which is the right shape for a plugin\nthat reports the problem and waits for a human. Where no human may be coming\nthat is the wrong terminal state: a container that lost a transient boot race\nstays down until someone restarts the plugin, and on a boat that can be weeks.\n\nretryForever runs a unit of work until it succeeds — 15s doubling to a 120s\nceiling, no attempt cap. ManagedContainer takes it as readinessRetry, off by\ndefault so existing consumers are unaffected. Each attempt re-runs start()\nwhole: ensureRunning is idempotent, and the address is re-resolved every time\nbecause a container that only just came up may bind a different host port.\n\nExported standalone as well, because the same policy applies to work this\nlibrary knows nothing about — signalk-backup needs it for its external-server\nmode, which has no container at all.\n\nTwo details are load-bearing rather than incidental:\n\n- Each ATTEMPT is serialized, not the whole loop. A retry sleeping between\n  attempts must not hold the lifecycle lock, or stop() would queue behind a\n  backoff that never ends and the plugin could not be shut down.\n- The backoff timer is unref''d. A loop that never gives up will almost always\n  have a pending timer at shutdown, and a ref''d one would keep the Signal K\n  process alive waiting to retry something nobody is listening to.\n\nA cancelled ContainerHelperError propagates instead of being retried, since\nretrying it would outlive the stop that caused it.\n\nCo-authored-by: dirkwa <dirkwahrtheit@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"c1b9fbc151a6671fb3490c4eab7cf02328fc6acf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hoeken/signalk-container-helper/git/trees/c1b9fbc151a6671fb3490c4eab7cf02328fc6acf"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hoeken/signalk-container-helper/git/commits/37c782613b8899e31818081c23b95c7f7402d18c","verification":{"payload":"tree c1b9fbc151a6671fb3490c4eab7cf02328fc6acf\nparent fb58322d979f801c04f0e3053191f96c395c5ea4\nauthor Dirk Wahrheit <86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com> 1786401223 +1200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786401223 +1200\n\nfeat(retry): add retryForever and ManagedContainer readinessRetry (#32)\n\nstart() throws once when bring-up fails, which is the right shape for a plugin\nthat reports the problem and waits for a human. Where no human may be coming\nthat is the wrong terminal state: a container that lost a transient boot race\nstays down until someone restarts the plugin, and on a boat that can be weeks.\n\nretryForever runs a unit of work until it succeeds — 15s doubling to a 120s\nceiling, no attempt cap. ManagedContainer takes it as readinessRetry, off by\ndefault so existing consumers are unaffected. Each attempt re-runs start()\nwhole: ensureRunning is idempotent, and the address is re-resolved every time\nbecause a container that only just came up may bind a different host port.\n\nExported standalone as well, because the same policy applies to work this\nlibrary knows nothing about — signalk-backup needs it for its external-server\nmode, which has no container at all.\n\nTwo details are load-bearing rather than incidental:\n\n- Each ATTEMPT is serialized, not the whole loop. A retry sleeping between\n  attempts must not hold the lifecycle lock, or stop() would queue behind a\n  backoff that never ends and the plugin could not be shut down.\n- The backoff timer is unref''d. A loop that never gives up will almost always\n  have a pending timer at shutdown, and a ref''d one would keep the Signal K\n  process alive waiting to retry something nobody is listening to.\n\nA cancelled ContainerHelperError propagates instead of being retried, since\nretrying it would outlive the stop that caused it.\n\nCo-authored-by: dirkwa <dirkwahrtheit@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqelHHCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAWSkQAJHlfEePt5ppMkGN5+CQcoGX\nW5kPlcOmMo5GP8/BunYKbYPeo0xZg+XgqEjZawZKJrYqb7maOGXn51pO1LJ89ZMt\n+TvlfuJp4VdoKZ+RIY1R7FqhxuwhBOq1FlYFI120up8LyDBXJu9IeWovgjhK2sow\nBpws7rECTKOiIDZaMtk9T8K1X4WoXyRq+/eppd78SEbXj093j5k7z9T9ib9iIdk1\njrY2td