"}],"sha":"37c782613b8899e31818081c23b95c7f7402d18c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hoeken/signalk-container-helper/commits/37c782613b8899e31818081c23b95c7f7402d18c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/86628605?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dirkwa","id":86628605,"login":"dirkwa","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg2NjI4NjA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hoeken/signalk-container-helper/commits/fb58322d979f801c04f0e3053191f96c395c5ea4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-10T22:24:47Z","email":"86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Dirk Wahrheit"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-10T22:24:47Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(util): walk error cause chains in errMsg (#31)\n\nundici''s fetch rejects with a bare `TypeError: fetch failed` and hides the\nactionable syscall in `err.cause`, so a consumer polling a containerized app\nreported \"fetch failed\" where it meant \"connect ECONNREFUSED 127.0.0.1:3010\".\nNode >= 20''s Happy Eyeballs rejects with an AggregateError carrying no message\nof its own, which rendered as the literal string \"AggregateError\".\n\nConsumers could not fix this downstream: the library renders errors to strings\ninternally (waitForHttpReady''s deadline message, fail()''s reported errors)\nbefore the Error crosses the API boundary, so the detail was already gone.\n\nerrMsg now follows .cause and flattens AggregateError, depth-capped at 4 and\nsafe against a cyclic errors array. All 17 internal call sites benefit; no API\nchange. Implementation and tests ported from signalk-backup, which had carried\nits own copy since the undici behaviour first bit it.\n\nCo-authored-by: dirkwa <dirkwahrtheit@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"409775e23bb12764afb212c7fc45ef2c3d47f25f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hoeken/signalk-container-helper/git/trees/409775e23bb12764afb212c7fc45ef2c3d47f25f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hoeken/signalk-container-helper/git/commits/fb58322d979f801c04f0e3053191f96c395c5ea4","verification":{"payload":"tree 409775e23bb12764afb212c7fc45ef2c3d47f25f\nparent 4ecca8b0bc0bbdc8f244d11ef3647b2ec733ecde\nauthor Dirk Wahrheit <86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com> 1786400687 +1200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786400687 +1200\n\nfix(util): walk error cause chains in errMsg (#31)\n\nundici''s fetch rejects with a bare `TypeError: fetch failed` and hides the\nactionable syscall in `err.cause`, so a consumer polling a containerized app\nreported \"fetch failed\" where it meant \"connect ECONNREFUSED 127.0.0.1:3010\".\nNode >= 20''s Happy Eyeballs rejects with an AggregateError carrying no message\nof its own, which rendered as the literal string \"AggregateError\".\n\nConsumers could not fix this downstream: the library renders errors to strings\ninternally (waitForHttpReady''s deadline message, fail()''s reported errors)\nbefore the Error crosses the API boundary, so the detail was already gone.\n\nerrMsg now follows .cause and flattens AggregateError, depth-capped at 4 and\nsafe against a cyclic errors array. All 17 internal call sites benefit; no API\nchange. Implementation and tests ported from signalk-backup, which had carried\nits own copy since the undici behaviour first bit it.\n\nCo-authored-by: dirkwa <dirkwahrtheit@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqek+vCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAryoQAJLxu4d2KGiDg8icJcnOvemK\nwvFlb6vqs3OslztriEsCBIeyLRkg0+SaF0V5M5iH4iCAGH7Us2q6oBDnARK88iPj\nZGvNdgHe1qF5pCwSxkfYeLevv94hf9IakGCcStWPiItDYyEnLMw0vUaE3WCjbkZ2\nCu65pPI57Ps7dWh3NwxtoJ9H9r7jXnqsvTly6o1GL1WEwFl7FstbjB6sNrjtfHcR\nSmD0xmMivBJvlIWc/Zz1zK0km5cQ2HFmrU1bj0Y/FT8oD3Q28yvsQA5+LJTyyXaS\nJgfeVQwzuumswsNo7q6tGuz9o5LJl5gqtAsfdlk7FNPsxogrIH6NLkgshi/QK4eC\ncASfnsPgCQrUh99y0ft1lZ7i8NSzPXUCYESg2gpP9N5h8OcqoIY35dW5129EgQX9\nJV3yjZ6oGicmkhb2KAuYqnXjmaUXjQKHP9KpEaNxz0HQCicdUdK6LHIV8oDj+NxV\nAxwUTM4n3wHzARV0hytG9L+70jxL/3bYz3ovjWoRH7rVX1vxl94Q/inXl/44c32W\nn5/tKZot57OPhbzwztV3oIkVJu8Xnbcq7zLu13VqObpQ0qP2bQsCK5QbvUyc9jZo\noPGBXppMIC6X5d+hDk0KIQ9rhlAskgRJZ+NhxpqVzgo7I1cUM6Tc/h76Zv90Crds\nylNvJCTZ71fbOdIUbvmF\n=fMPN\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-10T22:38:46Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/hoeken/signalk-container-helper/commit/fb58322d979f801c04f0e3053191f96c395c5ea4","node_id":"C_kwDOTgx649oAKGZiNTgzMjJkOTc5ZjgwMWMwNGYwZTMwNTMxOTFmOTZjMzk1YzVlYTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/hoeken/signalk-container-helper/commit/4ecca8b0bc0bbdc8f244d11ef3647b2ec733ecde","sha":"4ecca8b0bc0bbdc8f244d11ef3647b2ec733ecde","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hoeken/signalk-container-helper/commits/4ecca8b0bc0bbdc8f244d11ef3647b2ec733ecde"}],"sha":"fb58322d979f801c04f0e3053191f96c395c5ea4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hoeken/signalk-container-helper/commits/fb58322d979f801c04f0e3053191f96c395c5ea4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/86628605?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dirkwa","id":86628605,"login":"dirkwa","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg2NjI4NjA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hoeken/signalk-container-helper/commits/4ecca8b0bc0bbdc8f244d11ef3647b2ec733ecde/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-10T21:28:38Z","email":"86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Dirk Wahrheit"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-10T21:28:38Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"test(types): assert ContainerManagerApi name coverage (#30)\n\nContainerManagerApi was not covered by the types contract test, despite\nbeing the largest interface in the mirror and the one consumers actually\ncall. #25 added getContainerNofile, missing from the mirror since\nsignalk-container 1.25.3, and CI was green the whole time it was absent.\n\nA structural Equals cannot be used: canonical declares every member\nrequired, while the mirror marks feature-detected members optional so\nconsumers can probe older installs. Assert member names instead, in one\ndirection only (canonical minus mirror), so the mirror may still retain a\nmember a newer signalk-container has dropped.\n\nThe assertion constrains the missing-name union against never rather than\nwrapping it in Expect<Equals<...>>, so tsc names the drifted member in the\nerror instead of reporting \"''false'' does not satisfy ''true''\".\n\nAlso correct the file header: it claimed enforcement via the `typecheck`\nscript and vitest typecheck mode, but `typecheck` includes only src/ and\nvitest''s glob never matches *.test-d.ts. The real path is `typecheck:test`,\nwhich CI runs via `npm test`.\n\nCo-authored-by: dirkwa <dirkwahrtheit@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"1c4b12c2c1e041cfc661a2472c554c8f5d83f33c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hoeken/signalk-container-helper/git/trees/1c4b12c2c1e041cfc661a2472c554c8f5d83f33c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hoeken/signalk-container-helper/git/commits/4ecca8b0bc0bbdc8f244d11ef3647b2ec733ecde","verification":{"payload":"tree 1c4b12c2c1e041cfc661a2472c554c8f5d83f33c\nparent 00fe276c8178aea3c9a8b087c523b1f6914fd61c\nauthor Dirk Wahrheit <86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com> 1786397318 +1200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786397318 +1200\n\ntest(types): assert ContainerManagerApi name coverage (#30)\n\nContainerManagerApi was not covered by the types contract test, despite\nbeing the largest interface in the mirror and the one consumers actually\ncall. #25 added getContainerNofile, missing from the mirror since\nsignalk-container 1.25.3, and CI was green the whole time it was absent.\n\nA structural Equals cannot be used: canonical declares every member\nrequired, while the mirror marks feature-detected members optional so\nconsumers can probe older installs. Assert member names instead, in one\ndirection only (canonical minus mirror), so the mirror may still retain a\nmember a newer signalk-container has dropped.\n\nThe assertion constrains the missing-name union against never rather than\nwrapping it in Expect<Equals<...>>, so tsc names the drifted member in the\nerror instead of reporting \"''false'' does not satisfy ''true''\".\n\nAlso correct the file header: it claimed enforcement via the `typecheck`\nscript and vitest typecheck mode, but `typecheck` includes only src/ and\nvitest''s glob never matches *.test-d.ts. The real path is `typecheck:test`,\nwhich CI runs via `npm test`.\n\nCo-authored-by: dirkwa <dirkwahrtheit@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqekKGCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAARgwQADuK3T1M+t7d9XIClEhaNu8H\nGwj3XTUlO94DzuIhY7H2XB+Sz89zEH1uHou1xKgXtbgtWwWNkOr05suPT5HyQSdX\n+HrbdmTNvqJQ+VYaaFFzktV7HgbbOJiOdtdmQeefSf+9gnNcELFVdTcXGqfkxQ7q\nrlQI5Qh5aLqzv9jE5I+6J7cqGhlsW+qB3JEMhC/09R/ksft1ynEjsUclmgN8VCmA\nnLJ+ThoLUUG/uP3fwSRExzR6UfmJdW/lUXpsGOLUkgpkmNW/Q+Esdv+1ZonD+ahg\ngi8QMy7uFSugTPcmSzzleOlyJAZVu9ddWIKaj92VkrneaR6kArWdLTkJ7wxD8u7r\noq6G2rE4n9nc8Lj8b2pK8VhPAUiMWh4ATvPZVu4oWM1tKiZc1/YOxyP74UNdmUjJ\nvTilznrezyUM2kryelQMB6ANkfaJ97V3h/WaWCy6pFNLFtt/rK2K+mQaPsl1GZoM\npced4kJWRaBdU5SYVCgXptYj8VYmGtGwWFUpApNeG3I6T4KJxB6cM1EsoMeWM27A\n4a3x9rinOAam8+qX8Q9PX1dkP2F116fPHwGAIJSiX1XRdqpcLqcs3JTRGYIGFj5K\nO2SXtzrlv5RyNPPrH3cCdnaRnsSCL2ZgOHQ/F49+3a6x5371tlhfERA/Osk52k0O\nlssFIYBaU4reqdL3Rr26\n=ac3B\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-10T22:09:21Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-