om/dirkwa","id":86628605,"login":"dirkwa","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg2NjI4NjA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hoeken/signalk-container-helper/commits/23f6ef55864e59529a0ec57e57e3ca88cfd5bd89/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-10T18:30:53Z","email":"86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Dirk Wahrheit"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-10T18:30:53Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(ui): make collapsible section headers read as controls (#23)\n\nThe header button inherited sectionTitle''s muted #888, so a collapsed\nsection read as a caption rather than something clickable. A signalk-questdb\nuser reported a config field as uneditable when it was only collapsed\n(dirkwa/signalk-questdb#123); the field was a correct controlled input the\nwhole time.\n\nThe inline chrome moves into two exported styles: sectionToggle, which\noverrides the colour to #555 -- the same tone as label, i.e. the panel''s\nestablished \"this is an actual control\" colour -- and sectionMarker, an\n11px disclosure triangle up from 10px.\n\nThe old doc comment said the style \"resets the default button chrome so it\nstill reads as a section title\", which documented the defect precisely.\n\nEvery panel using CollapsibleSection picks this up. Tested against the style\ncontract rather than a renderer: the spread order is what makes the override\nload-bearing, and asserting it is what stops a future edit silently falling\nback to #888.\n\nCo-authored-by: dirkwa <dirkwahrtheit@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"a32ff061df14c15c425acebd9a6d0157aaf24850","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hoeken/signalk-container-helper/git/trees/a32ff061df14c15c425acebd9a6d0157aaf24850"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hoeken/signalk-container-helper/git/commits/23f6ef55864e59529a0ec57e57e3ca88cfd5bd89","verification":{"payload":"tree a32ff061df14c15c425acebd9a6d0157aaf24850\nparent 7963f2726a08fef1444ecc60844ada2bccf64a11\nauthor Dirk Wahrheit <86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com> 1786386653 +1200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786386653 +1200\n\nfix(ui): make collapsible section headers read as controls (#23)\n\nThe header button inherited sectionTitle''s muted #888, so a collapsed\nsection read as a caption rather than something clickable. A signalk-questdb\nuser reported a config field as uneditable when it was only collapsed\n(dirkwa/signalk-questdb#123); the field was a correct controlled input the\nwhole time.\n\nThe inline chrome moves into two exported styles: sectionToggle, which\noverrides the colour to #555 -- the same tone as label, i.e. the panel''s\nestablished \"this is an actual control\" colour -- and sectionMarker, an\n11px disclosure triangle up from 10px.\n\nThe old doc comment said the style \"resets the default button chrome so it\nstill reads as a section title\", which documented the defect precisely.\n\nEvery panel using CollapsibleSection picks this up. Tested against the style\ncontract rather than a renderer: the spread order is what makes the override\nload-bearing, and asserting it is what stops a future edit silently falling\nback to #888.\n\nCo-authored-by: dirkwa <dirkwahrtheit@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqehjdCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAdcAQAHVN2c743U0eojUzINkuQJS3\nJ0yYfmYp1eL8g3g5D39/IqPhYTaTQ46ltjWMpk+qBQNnDPTfgYSRnuPAaAfN3qqn\nyIPO1YcQIXE7NX6rMkZzy8nV8x5Rxw5QVqYipAWiiAnQOACQlBJ/2k5HK4NyBgUH\n/HcDNaaAlZSsqK2Ub2aNpDk5L7p9VIflYD3WOF7Yat72Zwj50y8ZPRMHPLRWnN+d\nKa1MWNmZQbQtz/+g