oeken","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hoeken/signalk-container-helper/commits/bc40d4b0e85ba2ff8953027b3c02e98780720133/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-25T21:04:46Z","email":"hoeken@gmail.com","name":"Zach Hoeken"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-25T21:04:46Z","email":"hoeken@gmail.com","name":"Zach Hoeken"},"message":"docs: ESM plugins must build their config panel as an ESM MF remote\n\nSignal K injects each configurator panel''s script tag based on the\nplugin''s package.json \"type\" field: \"type\": \"module\" packages get\n<script type=\"module\"> and the Admin UI then requires a real ESM\nfederation container (import() + get/init exports). The classic\n`library: { type: \"var\" }` remote the CJS reference plugins use loads\nsilently into module scope and the panel fails with the misleading\n''Module \"…\" is not available. Make sure the webapp is installed.'' —\ndiscovered integrating the /ui entrypoint into signalk-piper, which is\nESM like this library (and therefore like most of its consumers).\n\n- New \"ESM plugins must build an ESM remote\" section: the server''s\n  injection logic, both mismatch failure modes (silent no-exports for\n  ESM packages with a var remote, SyntaxError for CJS packages with an\n  ESM remote), the webpack recipe (outputModule + output.module +\n  library type \"module\"), a get/init verification one-liner, and\n  signalk-piper as a working example\n- New panel-conventions bullet cross-linking it\n- Scoped the \"no changes to the standard webpack config\" claim to\n  loaders — the output format does depend on the package''s module type","tree":{"sha":"15b54063f1102487f55d759127573a416a0ede99","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hoeken/signalk-container-helper/git/trees/15b54063f1102487f55d759127573a416a0ede99"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hoeken/signalk-container-helper/git/commits/bc40d4b0e85ba2ff8953027b3c02e98780720133","verification":{"payload":null